INT. CLOSED OBSERVATION TOWER - STAIRWELL LANDING - NIGHT

Concrete. One bulb. Rain in the vents.

AGENT RENATA VOSS (40s) crouches over a duffel bag. Zipper open. Cash, passports, a phone. Her breathing is slow, controlled.

Footsteps below. Heavy. Climbing.

She zips the bag. Stands. Back to the wall.

A figure rounds the landing. ELIAS MBEKI (50s), coat soaked, pistol low. He stops. Sees her. Neither moves.

Behind him, DEPUTY HANNAH OAKES (30s), radio on her shoulder, edges up the steps.

ELIAS
(low)
Renata.

RENATA
Elias.

HANNAH
Hands where I can see them!

ELIAS ^
Hannah, stand down.

Renata's eyes flick to the bag. His follow. Both lunge at once. Elbows, knees, a snarl. The bag skids across the concrete.

She hooks his leg. He drives her into the railing. It groans.

The pistol clatters down the stairs. Hannah ducks aside as it passes her boots.

He gets a forearm across her throat. She bites his wrist. He yanks free.

Hannah raises her weapon. Shaky. Trying to find a clean line.

HANNAH
Stop! Both of you!

They don't. Then a SIREN builds outside. Red and blue strobe through the vent slats.

They freeze, still tangled. Breathing hard. Rain drums on the roof.

DOCTOR AMARA LINDQVIST (60s, civilian) appears at the top of the stairs, hands raised, trembling, a thermos in one.

AMARA
(breathless)
Please. I only came up to fix the lamp.

Nobody answers. The siren fades past.

Renata lets go first. He follows. They step apart.

ELIAS
(tired)
It's over.

RENATA
It never is.

She sits down on the stairs, defeated, and holds out her wrists.
